I didn't have TeleControl on the first valk or any easy way to get it,
and I just sort of gave up. Entirely right on the second one - got
annihilated in Moloch's Sanctum by Rodney's summoning. This was AFTER I
killed absolutely everything in there with a cockatrice corpse. Right
on the third one too - he got my BoH, which had all my wands of digging
and such in it. The only implement I had was the pickaxe from the
Elvenking in Earth, and that is not a fun tool to dig with, especially
when you've got no idea WHERE the portal is.

You're also right on me going Lawful, I almost always do (mostly
because I like the way you can easily boost your alignment and also
because it makes the beginning and end easier - dwarves won't attack
you in the mines, and Archons won't attack you should you run into
one). Magicbane blasting me all the time is quite annoying, and I
really didn't foresee that happening. All I wanted was an easy
anti-curse measure.

As for boosting stats, I got another point of dex from Surtur's area
through exercise, and found another scroll of enchant armor, bringing
my total to -46 (the gauntlets are now -4). Hopefully I'll find an
Incubus somewhere to dance with, because the one thing that does seem
to be scarce in my game is potions of healing. Usually I've got a
million of them and just quaff them all on my way down Gehennom. Then
again, usually I don't have -46 AC before the Valley of the Dead.

I think I'm going to go with a combination of Magicbane and Mjollnir
for the end-game. Mjollnir for things like the graveyards in Moloch's
Sanctum, Magicbane for everything on the way up. This is to prevent
things (ESPECIALLY the BoH) from getting cursed by Rodney inadvertently
on the way up. Took your advice and boosted it to +4 using a couple
spare enchant weapon scrolls I had. I'm hoping to find another Polywand
on my way down so I can get it to +7.



